            "review_title": "Review at El Vino Wine & Restaurant",
            "review_text": "SHAPER12\nHanoi, Vietnam64 contributions\n1\nNeeds more English-speaking staff\nMay 2019 • Friends\nI went to El Vino to meet a friend for a drink. We had never been there before and wanted to check it out. I arrived before my friend and wanted to find a nice place for us to sit. I don't speak Vietnamese and it was really difficult to communicate. There were at least four people who were all trying to help and it got a little frustrating and felt unwelcoming. I was stopped by someone at the entrance and then by two people on the stairs. The restaurant was nearly empty with the exception of one guy at the bar, two couples in the dining area and a private party going on on the top floor. The area of Hanoi where the restaurant is located is a haven for expats and English speakers so it would be good for them to employ staff that can understand and speak English better. I think that would go a long way to welcoming the many expat residents in the area.\nRead more\nWritten May 26, 2019\nLinh Nguyen\nDear SHAPER12,\n\nWe appreciate for your review and sharing the details of your experience.\n\nThe related department managers have been informed about the problems you have mentioned. Hereafter we will be more attentive and will definitely take actions to your feedback for further improvements, including necessary English training for our staff. \n\nWe sincerely hope to have the pleasure of welcoming you back, assuring our best service and attention.\n\nWith kind regards,\nLinh Nguyen\nSales & Marketing Manager\nRead more\nWritten June 3, 2019\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
