            "review_text": "sandflopper j\nCaerleon, United Kingdom225 contributions\n1\nExcellent food and service though perhaps too much for some pockets\nMar 2019 • Couples\nA lovely top class international restaurant with the most fabulous wine list. We were treated wonderfully by the patron. My lobster bisque was to die for as was my delicious T bone steak with Arugula salad. My wife was equally thrilled with crab cakes (delicious but large) followed by Thai spaghetti. I was tempted to get bankrupt by ordering a bottle of Chateau Cheval Blanc, but wise counsel prevailed and we had an excellent Argentinian Malbec. Great spot overlooking Westlake opposite the Sheraton, we dined at the front and it was just lovely.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 15, 2019\nLinh Nguyen\nMany thanks for your positive feedback following your recent visit with us at El Vino Wine & Restaurant and I was delighted to read that you enjoyed your meal with us and all the service and restaurant atmosphere met your expectations. Please do come back in summer and see us again soon. \n\nKind regards, \nLinh Nguyen\nSales & Marketing Manager\nRead more\nWritten April 11, 2019\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
